---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CopyEmail from '../components/CopyEmail.astro';
import { link } from '../lib/links';

const updated = '30 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — MacAway"
  description="What MacAway keeps, and where. Everything stays on your Mac. The only thing the app contacts is its own update feed."
>
  <article class="doc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="doc-head">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          This describes MacAway and this website as they are built today. When either
          changes, this page changes with it, and so does the date below.
        </p>
        <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>In short</h2>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>
            The app collects nothing and sends nothing about you. The only thing it contacts is
            its own update feed.
          </li>
          <li>It asks for one permission: Bluetooth.</li>
          <li>It never reads, stores or types your password. It locks; you unlock.</li>
          <li>This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the app keeps</h2>
        <p>Everything MacAway remembers stays on your Mac, in its own settings.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>The devices you follow.</strong> The name macOS already gives each one, and
            an identifier that means nothing on any other Mac.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your settings.</strong> Which mode you chose, any numbers you changed,
            whether MacAway is paused, and whether it starts at login.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When your free days started</strong>, and, once you buy, your licence key.
            The key is checked on your Mac. Checking it needs no internet.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The locks from the past week.</strong> When each one happened, which device
            caused it, and why. Older ones are dropped.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          MacAway also writes to the log macOS keeps for every app, which is how a problem gets
          found. That log stays on your Mac too.
        </p>
        <p>
          None of it goes anywhere. Nothing MacAway keeps about you or your devices is ever
          sent. When you choose <strong>Buy</strong> or <strong>Send feedback</strong>, MacAway
          opens that page in your browser, the way any link does.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Checking for updates</h2>
        <p>
          MacAway asks this website whether a newer version exists, and tells it which version
          you already have so the answer is right. It sends nothing about you or the devices
          you follow. The request reaches GitHub&rsquo;s servers, which keep their own logs
          including your IP address, exactly as reading this page does.
        </p>
        <p>
          MacAway asks your permission the first time it runs before checking on its own, and
          you can change your mind afterwards. Either way you can check whenever you like, from
          the gear in the menu.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What it asks for</h2>
        <p>
          Bluetooth, and nothing else. MacAway uses it to read how strong the signal from your
          device is, once a second.
        </p>
        <p>
          It does not ask for your camera, your microphone, your location, your contacts, your
          files or Accessibility.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
          This page is a set of static files on GitHub Pages. No cookies, no analytics, nothing
          loaded from anyone else. The typeface comes from this site rather than a font network,
          so opening this page tells nobody else that you were here.
        </p>
        <p>
          GitHub keeps its own server logs, including visitors&rsquo; IP addresses. Those logs
          are GitHub&rsquo;s, not ours, and are covered by <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement"
            >GitHub&rsquo;s privacy statement</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>MacAway is made by Robert Brada.</p>
        <p>
          The app keeps nothing about you anywhere but on your own Mac, where it is already
          yours to read and to delete. If you have a question about any of this, write to{' '}
          <CopyEmail />
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="back"><a class="text-link" href={link('')}>&larr; Back to MacAway</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    padding-block: clamp(6rem, 10vw, 8rem) clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .doc :global(.wrap) > * {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .doc-head {
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .doc-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 3.75rem);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .doc section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .doc h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .doc p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .doc ul {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .doc ul.plain {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .doc ul.plain li {
    padding-left: 1.6rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .doc ul.plain li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.62em;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--green-deep);
  }

  .doc strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 620;
  }

  .doc a {
    color: var(--green-deep);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .back {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .text-link {
    color: var(--green-deep);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .text-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
